Alembic migrations for the Protokoll E-Befischung database.

The scripts live here because coding-standards.md puts schema changes under
database/. The configuration that drives them, alembic.ini, lives in backend/,
which is where the virtual environment is and therefore where the commands run.

Every command below is run from backend/, with the Compose stack up:

  alembic current                     which migration the database is on
  alembic history                     every migration, newest first
  alembic upgrade head                apply everything not yet applied
  alembic downgrade -1                undo the most recent one
  alembic revision -m "what changed"  a new empty migration, written by hand
  alembic revision --autogenerate -m "what changed"
                                      a new migration drafted from the models

An autogenerated migration is a draft, never a finished answer. Alembic does not
see check constraints, gets server defaults wrong, and will generate a drop for
any model it was not told about. Read every generated file before keeping it.

Migrations are never run automatically when the application starts. Where the
service runs as more than one container they would all migrate at once. Applying
them is a deploy step somebody runs, which is also what makes a failure visible
instead of turning into a restart loop.
